  "description": "Route finding on the track network (the network counterpart of train-route.json, ARCHITECTURE decision 51). A line a (1024, 4096) - b - c (3072, 4096), edges e1 and e2 of 1024, ends at a balloon loop: at the turnout c two straight edges leave east, e3 to p (11264, 4352) and e4 to q (11264, 3840), each 8196 long and 1 in 32 off the line, so both join e2 but not each other; the hairpin e5, a cubic from p with control points (13312, 4416) and (13312, 3776) to q, 3214 long, leaves p and arrives at q along them, so it joins e3 at p and e4 at q. e6 runs alone from x (6144, 7168) to y (7168, 7168). A route (pathToNode) starts at the end of the edge the train is on and ends where it first reaches the node: the least total length, and among routes of that length the one whose edges come first in ascending order at each node, compared step by step; it never turns straight back along an edge and may loop. From 512 along e1 going forward: to p e2, e3; to q e2, e4; to a, behind the train, round the loop and back, e2, e3, e5, e4 backward, e2 backward, e1 backward (the loop the other way, e4, e5 backward, e3 backward, is exactly as long, and e3 comes before e4 at c). Facing a's dead end there is no route. From 4000 along e3, to q: e5. Heading along its own edge for the node, or already at it, the route is empty; to b from e2 it goes round the loop. No route to the unconnected y, to an unknown node, or from an unknown edge or an offset past the edge's end. Local 1 follows the loop route at 30000 a minute and ends at a, the rest of the minute unused; facing a's dead end it has no route to c until it is reversed, and then follows e2 to c. Track costs 1000 a tile of edge, rounded up: 1, 1, 9, 9, 4 and 1.",
